ACTIVATING DARK MODE
DARK MODE FOR INVENTORY EDITOR: Edit--&gt;Settings--&gt;General Settings--&gt;Untick "Disable Dark Mode support--&gt;Restart the editor
DARK MODE FOR NOTEPAD++: Settings--&gt;Style Configurator--&gt;Select theme--&gt;Deep Black
TO GET RID OF START-UP LOGOS: In the ACV directory, go to the videos folder. Delete the following: ANVIL_logo, Blackscreen, PC_AMC_Ryzen, Ubisoft_logo, mx folder and en folder (or the folder of whatever language you play the game in)
=========================================
INSTRUCTIONS &amp; GUIDES
README by HK26
This will instruct you on how to use the inventory editor. Guides are separated by letter, steps by number. Go through this ReadMe if you are stuck, having issues with the table, or if this
is your first time using it.
***ONE OR BOTH OF GUIDES A &amp; B MUST BE COMPLETED, DO NOT SKIP THEM! IF YOU DON'T, ALL OF THE HELIX ITEMS YOU HAVE CHEATED INTO THE GAME WILL DISAPPEAR FROM YOUR INVENTORY UPON LOADING A SAVE!
THE DLL FILE OR PATCHING THE GAME WITH THE EDITOR WILL PREVENT THESE ITEMS FROM DISAPPEARING***
====== A. INSTRUCTIONS ON HOW TO PATCH YOUR GAME VIA DLL ***GUIDES A, B, OR BOTH REQUIRED*** ======
1. Make sure you have the latest Cheat Engine installed
2. Place d3d9.dll in your game directory
3. Done! Your cheated Helix items should no longer disappear upon loading a save.
====== B. INSTRUCTIONS ON HOW TO PATCH YOUR GAME VIA PATCH ***GUIDES A, B, OR BOTH REQUIRED*** ======
1. Make sure you have the latest version of Cheat Engine installed
2. Start up your game, stay at the main menu
3. Start up the inventory editor
4. There should be a blinking icon in the upper left corner. Click it, and select AC Valhalla as the process.
5. A prompt will show up, click yes
6. Check the "ACTIVATE ME" box, and close the comment that pops up
7. Go to +Inventory // GetItems---&gt;***Inventory: patch to keep cheated items***---&gt;patch file
8. You will be asked to restart the game. Probably best to close the inventory editor, as well
9. Restarting the game will have applied the patch. You can go through step 7 again to check if the patch is there, it should say that the game has been patched
10. Done! Your cheated Helix items should no longer disappear upon loading a save.
====== C. ACTIVATING THE TABLE FOR USE ***REQUIRED AT EVERY TABLE START UP*** ======
1. Start up your game and load a save
2. When you are in game, load the inventory editor
3. In the upper left corner there should be a blinking icon. Click on it
4. It'll ask you to select a process. Pick AC Valhalla in the "Applications" tab, then hit open
5. Say yes to the prompt following this
6. Check the box next to [ACTIVATE ME], then press close
7. Done! Editor is ready to use. You'll need to repeat this process every time you start up the game. You can start the editor in the main menu,
but you must be loaded into the game in order for it to add Helix items or read your inventory
====== D. GETTING A SINGLE ITEM ======
1. To get a single item, first find its hash id with the provided hash id list.
2. Hash ids look something like this: 00000B32367FFA5E They are a combination of letters and numbers.
3. Copy the hash id
4. Go to Inventory-&gt;Inventory: GetItem-&gt;+Single GetItem
5. In Hash ID, replace the Value with the hash id you have copied
6. Check Toggle to Get Item, and it will then be added to your inventory
====== E. GETTING HELIX ITEMS ======
1. First make sure that either A &amp; B, or both, have been done. If the game isn't patched or the dll file present, you will lose cheated Helix items upon loading a save.
2. Go to +Inventory // GetItems--&gt;+Inventory: GetItem--&gt;+Bulk GetItem: Helix Store/Prime...
3. Click the box next to your desired items, and you should see it has been added to your inventory. Some items are not immediately apparent that they have been added, or have a sound associated with unlocking them.
====== F. EDITING INVENTORY QUANTITY ======
1. Go to +Inventory // GetItems--&gt;+Inventory: EditQuantity
2. If you're at the main menu, you'll see a lot of question marks. You need to load a save file in order for these numbers to update
3. When you've loaded in, you should see the value column reflect their in-game counterparts
4. To change them to what you want, just simply edit the value in the table by double clicking the number. You should see a box pop up asking for the value. Once that's done, they'll change in game.
5. If there are question marks instead of numbers for some currencies, it is because you have zero in game. You either need to earn some of that currency in the game, add a single one with its hash id in the previous instruction,
or you have not accessed the section of the game that introduces those currencies (For example, Texts requires you to have started Wrath of the Druids DLC and begun foreign trade with Azar). You can also go to
+Inventory // GetItems--&gt;+Inventory: GetItem--&gt;+Bulk: GetItem--&gt;Utilities section to unlock those currencies/materials
====== G. DEALING WITH DUPLICATES ======
1. Go to your inventory within the editor. +Inventory // GetItems--&gt;+Inventory: EditQuantity--&gt;+All Inventory Items
2. Find the item you wish to delete. If you can't see names properly, drag the right hand side of the "Description" column at the top of the editor, and move it to the right to widen out names
3. Change its value from 1 to 0
4. Once you have completed this for any and all items you want to be rid of, you must make a new save
5. Reload the save you just made. When you're back in, you should see that the items have disappeared from your inventory and the editor. Editor will need to be reloaded as well in order to reflect the new in-game inventory
6. This can also be done if you want multiple of the same item. Just change its number from 1 to your desired number. Repeat steps 4 and 5. You should now have the amount of items you want in your inventory.
====== H. OPEN SHOP DIRECTLY ***THIS BOOSTER DOES NOT CURRENTLY WORK*** ======
1. This will let you open any shop interface no matter your location; no more needing to return to Ravensthorpe to change tattoos or gear appearance
2. Go to +Boosters // Trainers--&gt;+Open Shop Directly
3. Check the shop you wish to open, and you should see the shop menu come up in your game
4. As a word of warning, the game crashes if you don't close the shop using the inventory editor (hitting the check box again)
====== I. TELEPORTING: TRAINER BY aSwedishMagyar ======
***BEFORE USING, BE AWARE THAT TELEPORTING DOES NOT ACCOUNT FOR GEOGRAPHY/LOCATION. YOU MAY END UP IN THE AIR OR UNDER THE MAP. IT MIGHT NOT WORK PERFECTLY EVERY TIME***
1. Teleportation options can be found along this path: +Boosters // Trainers --&gt;+More Trainers by aSwedishMagyar--&gt;Scripts--&gt;Teleport Related Scripts
2. The options here are fairly self explanatory. The easiest one to figure out is "Teleport to Waypoint"
3. First, place a waypoint on your map. AC Valhalla lets you place 3 waypoints at once, and are numbered on your map.
4. Tick the "Teleport to Waypoint" box. It will then ask for the number of the waypoint you placed
5. When you click OK, you should then teleport to that waypoint's location.
6. If you find that teleporting is not working, then you may need to restart your game and inventory editor. This was the only fix I could find at the moment
====== J. GETTING GOLD MEDALS IN MASTERY CHALLENGES ======
***I PERSONALLY DO NOT RECOMMEND TRYING THIS METHOD UNTIL YOU ARE MORE FAMILIAR WITH THE EDITOR***
1. Load into a mastery challenge, and earn any amount of points
2. Take the points number, and put it into Value in the upper right side of the inventory editor (can't be in Compact Mode, next to Hex with a check box); then initiate a scan
3. You'll see a whole bunch of numbers show up in the table (Address, Value, Previous)
4. Earn more points in the mastery challenge
5. Take that new number, and initiate another scan. The numbers will start narrowing down
6. Keep doing this until you have 2-4 entries
7. Copy/paste those entries into the editor (anywhere below Boosters is good). You should see some new options show up, with a box for you to check off (don't check it off yet)
8. In the value for these new options, change it to 1000. Then, hit the check box. In game, the current number of points you have may stop going up, which is a sign you've done it correctly
9. Finish the mastery challenge however you wish. When you get to the results screen you should see that you have earned 1000/1000 points!
10. Rinse and repeat for other challenges. I know it's long and complicated, but it does work and could save hours of headaches being stuck on a challenge. This method worked for me and let me unlock the "A True Master" achievement
CREDIT FOR THIS METHOD GOES TO Ninomae Tako'nis OVER AT FEARLESSREVOLUTION!
====== K. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION ======
1. If Helix items disappear, double check that you have either placed the dll file into your game's directory, or have correctly patched the game with the inventory editor
2. This is a community effort, and as such, it is not perfect. Crashes or freezing can happen. We are cheating and hacking the game, after all.
3. When AC Valhalla gets official updates, it can cause parts of the editor to stop working or crash. Some official updates can cause items to disappear, too. Members at FearlessRevolution work as fast as they are able to fix it.
4. You can find everything in your inventory under +Inventory // GetItems--&gt;+Inventory: EditQuantity-&gt;+All Inventory Items; you can edit your inventory from there if you wish.
5. The inventory editor you use must match your version of the game. v1.4.0 of the editor will only work for game version v1.4.0, 1.30 with 1.30, etc
6. As with all things cheating or modding, be careful! Make backups of your saves and game. Verify/Repair the game if you encounter crashes or need a clean slate. Corrupted saves are known to happen and may not always be reversible.
7. I use Forger mods alongside this inventory editor and they seem to work together with no issue.
8. Cheat Engine must always be at its latest version in order for tables to work.
9. A link is provided at the top of this file for those who use a cracked version of the game. Tables made for "normal" editions will not work with a cracked game.
10. Useful edits, additions, or fixes made by users are encouraged and recognized. You are free to share and post the table as long as proper credit is given; do not erase the work of others. Theft will not be tolerated.
11. Your anti-virus/browser protection service could prevent you from downloading or using Cheat Engine. Take the steps necessary to allow Cheat Engine to be used on your PC if this happens.
12. Using Cheat Engine and the inventory editor in administrator mode is recommended
